&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Corporate Legal Counsel&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Corporate Legal Counsel within Corporate Legal’s Advisory team, you will primarily be working on matters relevant to Adyen’s public listing in the Netherlands. You will also help the team facilitate our major corporate projects such as, capital markets enquiries, complex corporate projects and corporate development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a strategic role that is important to sound corporate governance practices and continued sustainable growth. The role requires someone effective at cross collaboration, who excels at decision making in a fast-moving complex environment. Knowledge of and comfort with the Market Abuse Regulation is imperative to success. The counsel will drive discussions and decisioning on disclosure matters as well as advise on public filings and equity matters. The role forms part of Adyen’s larger corporate practice which covers corporate governance, litigation and disputes and corporate development. The corporate legal team is currently centered in Amsterdam and the United States but Adyen is a global company with offices, entities, and boards all over the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and advise on public filings as well as other disclosure documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Providing legal support and internal training on other corporate law matters as required, such as Mergers &amp;amp; Acquisitions, corporate development and other corporate legal initiatives.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage insider trading and conflict of interest inquiries, procedures, and policies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure compliance with the Market Abuse Regulation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the disclosure committee, driving strategic disclosure reviews and determinations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Investor Relations and Communications on disclosure matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise on equity structures and incentive plans in partnership with HR and Rewards teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consult with regulators and financial authorities such as the AFM.&lt;/li&gt;
