&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engineering Manager - Debit Card Payments NORAM&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Engineering Manager based in Chicago, you will lead a team of software engineers responsible for building the leading Debit Card Payments platform in NORAM. Your mission is to build the most competitive debit platform in the region: optimized for least-cost routing, engineered for maximum throughput, and trusted by NORAM&#39;s largest enterprise merchants for unmatched reliability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work closely with Product Managers and Engineering teams to deliver new functionality across the Card Payments domain. As a people leader, you will champion an inclusive environment, coach engineers through continuous growth, and shape technical direction within one of Adyen&#39;s core payment domains.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Authoring Adyen&#39;s Debit Card Payments strategy in NORAM, balancing product delivery with long-term platform scalability, resilience, and maintainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead by example, by setting the right context, and by helping teammates do their best work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach and mentor a diverse team of software engineers, prioritizing psychological safety, clear feedback, and long-term career growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a high-performing engineering culture built on ownership, collaboration, and continuous learning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Product Managers to translate business priorities into scalable technical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide architectural discussions, champion high engineering standards, and empower engineers to own technical solutions end-to-end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a track record of leading and developing software engineering teams, fostering a culture grounded in ownership and collaboration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy coaching engineers through technical mentorship, regular feedback, and career development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a strong software engineering background building large-scale, distributed systems in Java or similar backend technologies.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortably jumping into architecture reviews, unblocking technical hurdles, or guiding code reviews when your team faces complex, high-priority releases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy leading technical discussions, facilitating architectural decisions, and balancing engineering quality with business priorities coming from Product Managers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You thrive in cross-functional, globally distributed settings and adapt your communication thoughtfully across regions and cultures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building payment systems or working within the cards payments ecosystem (e.g. authorisation, routing, card schemes, issuer/acquirer integrations) is highly desirable and considered a big plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
