&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GL Accountant:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Adyen is looking for a General Ledger Accountant to join our Group Finance team in Amsterdam. In this role, you aren’t just &quot;processing numbers&quot; , you are the engine behind our Record-to-Report (R2R) cycle for Operational Expenses. You will act as the critical link between business operations and financial data, ensuring that as Adyen scales, our financial integrity remains rock-solid.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will move beyond simple data entry to maintain a holistic &quot;risk mindset,&quot; proactively identifying vulnerabilities and anomalies before they ever hit a report. Being part of a centralized Finance Operations team means you’ll be working in the engine room of a listed financial institution, where your work directly impacts our global trial balance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;R2R Ownership: Act as the detail layer for Operational Expenses, owning the accuracy of GL bookings and ensuring a clean Trial Balance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accounting Control: Apply rigorous controls to the P2P and R2R cycle. You’ll validate data flowing from FinOps, manage supplier accruals, and reconcile prepaid assets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High-Value Oversight: Act as the financial gatekeeper for high-value transactions, performing due diligence to ensure accuracy and relieving Financial Controllers of transactional approvals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Risk &amp;amp; Anomaly Detection: Regularly review the full ledger to detect trends or vulnerabilities, acting as the first line of defense for data integrity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Asset &amp;amp; Lease Management: Manage the Fixed Asset Register, including capitalization, depreciation, and executing lease accounting (IFRS 16) entries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intercompany &amp;amp; Reporting: Manage intercompany bookings and reconciliations, perform month-end variance analysis to validate OpEx trends, and support internal/external audits.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced: You have a solid background with at least three years of experience in GL accounting, specifically within P2P cycles and R2R processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detail-Oriented &amp;amp; Analytical: You are passionate about balance sheet integrity and &quot;getting it right the first time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative: You enjoy working with multiple stakeholders, from FinOps to various stakeholders such as Controllers and Tax lawyers, to ensure smooth financial reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive: You question the status quo and look for ways to automate or improve processes as we grow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adaptable: You can manage multiple projects, from IFRS 16 lease entries to intercompany reconciliations, without losing focus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
