&lt;h4&gt;Global Partner Engineering Manager, Payments&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Adyen is seeking a Global Manager for the Payments Partner Engineering team. This role requires a leader with a solid technical foundation, deep operational instincts, and a proven ability to build and develop high-performing teams. You will be responsible for the health of Adyen&#39;s payment partner integrations — spanning global card schemes, banks, wallets, local and alternative payment methods — and for evolving the Partner Engineering function to reduce reactive operational work to proactively addressing partner integration health.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the leader of the global Payments Partner Eng team, you will manage a team of Payment Partner Engineers who serve as Adyen&#39;s technical point of accountability for payment partner integrations. Your goal will be to drive integration reliability and performance across Adyen&#39;s global payment method portfolio, while building the tools, processes, and capabilities that allow the team to scale. This position requires a blend of leadership, technical and payments domain depth, strategic thinking, and the ability to influence both internal stakeholders and external payment partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is critical in ensuring Adyen&#39;s payment partner integrations meet the reliability and performance standards that underpin our merchant value proposition. The ideal candidate has led technical, cross-functional teams in complex environments, understands payments and API-based integrations, and brings a proactive, high-agency mindset to building a team and function from a still-early stage.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, mentor, and coach a global team of Payment Partner Engineers, fostering their growth and ensuring they are effective technical counterparts to Adyen&#39;s payment partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and drive a vision for the Paments Partner Engineering function — shifting the team&#39;s center of gravity from reactive issue management toward proactive partnership, performance ownership, and operational leverage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own integration health across Adyen&#39;s payment method portfolio, with accountability for reliability, performance (auth rates, settlement, disputes, etc.), and the team’s service model to internal and external stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive strategic architectural recommendations to ensure partners optimally integrate with Adyen, maximizing value for Adyen’s merchant customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally with Product, Engineering, Commercial, Compliance, and Reliability teams to represent the &quot;technical voice of the partner&quot; and drive action on integration issues and improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and maintain direct relationships with payment partners at a senior level, including participation in QBRs, joint business planning, and escalation management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use Adyen&#39;s planning processes to secure resources, define team structure, and drive alignment with senior stakeholders on prioritization and team direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of direct line management experience of technical or hybrid technical/operational teams, with a track record of hiring, developing, and managing senior individual contributors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of payments — familiarity with card schemes, payment method integrations, and API-based payment flows is strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with technical concepts at the API and systems level; able to engage credibly with engineers and technical partners without needing to be a hands-on software engineer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience driving operational improvements — identifying the root causes of recurring issues and building sustainable processes, tooling, or automation to address them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communicator and cross-functional influencer; comfortable navigating ambiguity and driving alignment across Product, Engineering, Commercial, and external partner teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build and maintain trusted relationships with senior internal stakeholders and payment partner counterparts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High agency: you don&#39;t wait for direction. You identify opportunities, form a point of view, get alignment, and move.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
