&lt;p&gt;Adyen is looking for a hands-on and proactive HR Business Partner to support our growing New York office. In this role, you will be the primary HR point of contact for local leadership and the &quot;eyes and ears&quot; on the ground.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will act as a trusted advisor across the entire employee lifecycle, ensuring our New York teams are supported, engaged, and aligned with the Adyen Formula. This role is perfect for someone who loves to &quot;connect the dots&quot;, bridging the gap between global HR initiatives and local execution while navigating the day-to-day needs of a fast-paced office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based in New York and works in close collaboration with the North America and Global People teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the go-to HR partner for New York Team Leads and Managers, providing coaching on leadership effectiveness, team dynamics, and people leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&quot;Connect the dots&quot; across different functions in the NY office to ensure office-wide engagement, and a strong sense of community.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive local execution of performance management, enabling managers to have high-quality growth conversations and effective feedback loops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide support for employee relations matters, ensuring fair and consistent application of policies and a healthy work environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with HR Centers of Expertise and the wider NA HRBP team to implement people initiatives that fit the New York context.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use local people data to identify trends, anticipate challenges, and suggest improvements to the local employee experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of HRBP experience, ideally in a fast-paced tech or high-growth environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You naturally build relationships across all levels and departments; you enjoy being visible and accessible in the office.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable jumping from a high-level talent discussion to a practical day-to-day HR task without missing a beat.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a proven ability to coach first-time managers and Team Leads through the complexities of leading people.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a &quot;builder&quot; mindset and look for ways to simplify processes rather than just following a handbook.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can articulate fact-based solutions clearly and handle sensitive conversations with high emotional intelligence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The annual base salary range for this role is $145,000 - $195,000; to learn more about our compensation philosophy, please click&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/11U2tgFev7p271JMQWMApZjtpJ3pGHNES7EvscXnsH3k/edit?usp=sharing&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;here&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
