&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve got at least 3+ years’ experience working as a HR Business partner with managers and leaders in a people partnering role at a high-pace company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have an understanding and expertise of Dutch and European local labor related legislation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a strong sense of self and build trust quickly to become a trusted business advisor at different levels of the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are able to question the status quo with managers and work with them to define new solutions to old problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are able to discuss people&#39;s challenges and implications driving local initiatives (ex. retention, engagement, performance, compensation, labor matters, etc.) to influence local leaders to make the best decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re hands-on, but know how to collaborate and prioritize (constantly looking for how things can be done more simply or automated)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re excited to try new approaches, do things differently, and aren’t afraid to “build as you go”&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have the ability to execute the global and functional people strategy ensuring alignment with regional/local culture and practices and partnering with local leadership&lt;/li&gt;
