&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Commercial Partnerships Manager, Private Equity and Venture Capital&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Commercial Partnerships Manager to own, scale, and lead our Financial Sponsor (PE/VC) Partnerships channel.&lt;br&gt;In this senior role, you will not only manage a portfolio of high-value PE/VC sponsors but will also be responsible for defining the regional sponsor strategy, building a repeatable playbook, and mentoring/guiding mid-level Commercial Partnership Managers on the team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will act as the principal liaison between top-tier global Private Equity firms, their portfolio companies (Portcos), and Adyen&#39;s executive leadership and commercial teams. Your goal is to institutionalize payment optimization and embedded finance as a core value-creation lever for our sponsor partners, driving high-velocity referrals and long-term enterprise growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic Leadership: Define and execute the commercial go-to-market strategy for a portfolio of PE/VC firms in North America. Design repeatable partnership motions for sponsor engagement, portfolio mapping, and co-selling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mega-Fund Management: Directly cultivate and scale relationships with Tier-1 mega-funds, large-cap PE firms, and influential Operating Partners (Tech/Digital/Value Creation).&lt;br&gt;Consultative Value Creation: Educate PE Deal and Operating teams on how Adyen&#39;s single global platform directly improves Portco EBITDA, optimizes working capital, and accelerates international expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-Functional Orchestration: Partner closely with Sales Leadership, Product, Marketing, and Account Management to ensure seamless execution, rapid onboarding of referred Portcos, and robust feedback loops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Metrics &amp;amp; Performance Tracking: Own the commercial target for defined PE/VC portfolio. Define, monitor, and report on key performance indicators (KPIs) including partner-originated pipeline, closed-won revenue, and channel ROI to senior executive stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team Mentorship &amp;amp; Coordination: Serve as a player-coach to uplevel and mentor junior/mid-level Commercial Partnership Managers on the team, helping them navigate complex sponsor dynamics and close deals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of commercial experience in fintech, enterprise software sales, corporate development, or consulting,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of direct experience working within or selling to the Private Equity / Venture Capital sponsor ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Payments Industry Expertise: Comprehensive understanding of the payments value chain (merchant acquiring, gateway, card issuing, and embedded financial services).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established Network: A strong, existing Rolodex of relationships with Private Equity Operating Partners, portfolio managers, or mid-to-large-cap corporate decision-makers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert Communicator: Highly polished presenter capable of building trust and driving strategic alignment with C-suite executives, PE Managing Directors, and portfolio board members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical Thinker: Comfort using financial models, data-driven frameworks, and EBITDA impact analyses to build compelling business cases for sponsors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Annual OTE ranges from $220,000-$295,000 inclusive of base salary and commercial bonus. This role has an additional equity component. This range is based on the candidate&#39;s experience, qualifications, and geographic location; to learn more about our compensation philosophy, please click&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/11U2tgFev7p271JMQWMApZjtpJ3pGHNES7EvscXnsH3k/edit?usp=sharing&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based in our New York office (hybrid, 3 days per week in-office).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
