&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Product Manager - In-Person Payments Reliability&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In-person payments at Adyen power the in-store experience for the biggest brands. As this solution is growing exponentially, we’re looking for a Senior Product Manager to join the Devices team and shape the platform capabilities that help us operate, release and scale our global in-person payments device fleet safely.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role sits in our Engineering Integrity area: the team that builds the testing, release, observability, certification and security capabilities used by our In-Person Payments product and engineering teams. These capabilities are critical to improving fleet stability, launch quality and developer velocity as our product portfolio expands across terminals, SoftPOS and bring-your-own-device solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The team focuses on building, enhancing and maintaining capabilities such as:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Emulators, robot testing and hardware-in-the-loop testing infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Release and rollout infrastructure for our fleet of devices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitoring and insights into device and payment application health&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Certification tooling, capacity and strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Security and compliance readiness across device software, release and certification flows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tools and processes that make launches safer, more predictable and easier to scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This is not a ticket-management role. It is not a pure delivery role. You will define the product direction for a broad, engineering-heavy platform area: understanding the teams that depend on these capabilities, setting clear priorities, defining success metrics and connecting the work to broader Payments and business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the product vision and roadmap for the platform capabilities that support fleet stability, testing, release, observability, certification and security readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product and Engineering leadership to build a broader vision for device fleet stability and reliability across In-Person Payments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn a broad engineering-led area into a clear product area with users, outcomes, priorities, trade-offs and measurable impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the product direction for testing infrastructure, including emulators, robot testing and hardware-in-the-loop setups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide tools built around the needs of the teams that use them, by understanding their workflows, pain points and release risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the product direction for release and rollout infrastructure, including staged rollouts, automated release signals and rollback tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make release processes across our fleet of devices safer, more automated and more predictable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the product direction for monitoring and fleet health insights: the data and tooling that help teams understand device and payment application health, detect issues early and act before merchants are impacted.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape the approach to continuous pre-certification tooling, capacity and strategy, so certification becomes a final validation step rather than a place where issues are found late.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Security, Certifications, Engineering, Product and vendor-facing teams to embed quality, compliance and release readiness earlier in the lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define clear metrics for product stability, launch quality, release confidence and adoption of the platform capabilities you own.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the roadmap is tied to clear business outcomes and aligned with the broader Payments and company strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge - You have a strong understanding of software delivery, testing, observability and release processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with technical platforms, infrastructure, developer tooling, reliability products or device platforms is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mindset - You are a self-starter who can create structure in an ambiguous environment and build product management for a technical area from the ground up.&lt;/li&gt;
